# Newsletter Playbook and SOP

## Objective

Build a newsletter that:

- Attracts the right audience
- Builds authority
- Generates qualified leads
- Educates customers
- Creates long-term value

---

## Step 1: Define the Reader

### Objective

Identify exactly who the newsletter is for.

### Actions

- Define one Ideal Customer Profile.
- Identify the reader's role, industry, company size, and business stage.
- List their recurring problems.
- Define what success looks like for them.

### Deliverable

A one-page reader profile.

### Why It Matters

Writing for an undefined audience produces generic content. A specific reader profile improves relevance and commercial alignment.

### Source

Jason Lemkin. *An Underused Strategy: Truly High Value Drip Marketing to Prospects.* SaaStr. 10 June 2019.

https://www.saastr.com/an-underused-strategy-truly-high-value-drip-marketing-to-prospects/

---

## Step 2: Define what Newsletter offers

### Objective

Give the reader a clear reason to subscribe.

### Action

Complete this statement:

> This newsletter helps **[specific audience]** achieve **[specific outcome]** by delivering **[distinctive value]**.

### Deliverable

A one-sentence newsletter positioning statement.

### Source

Emily Kramer. *The MKT1 Guide to Positioning.* MKT1 Newsletter. 12 June 2024.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/positioning-guide

---

## Step 3: Define Business Goals

### Objective

Clarify how the newsletter supports the business.

### Actions

Choose one primary objective and one secondary objective:

- Generate leads
- Build authority
- Educate customers
- Support product adoption
- Build community
- Increase brand awareness

### Deliverable

One primary objective, one secondary objective, and the metrics used to evaluate them.

### Sources

Emily Kramer. *MKT1 Guide to Annual Marketing Planning.* MKT1 Newsletter. 23 September 2024.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/annual-marketing-planning

Jason Lemkin. *10 Things That Always Work in Marketing.* SaaStr. 2024.

https://www.saastr.com/10-things-that-always-work-in-marketing-with-saastr-founder-and-ceo-jason-lemkin-part-1-pod-652-video/

---

## Step 4: Build Content Pillars

### Objective

Organise the newsletter around recurring themes.

### Actions

Choose three to five content pillars, such as:

- Growth
- Customer research
- Product marketing
- Case studies
- Artificial intelligence
- Pricing

### Deliverable

A documented list of approved content pillars.

### Why It Matters

Content pillars reduce random topic selection and make planning more consistent.

### Source

Emily Kramer. *MKT1 Guide to Annual Marketing Planning.* MKT1 Newsletter. 23 September 2024.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/annual-marketing-planning

---

## Step 5: Create a Content Calendar

### Objective

Plan newsletter production in advance.

### Actions

For each planned edition, document:

- Topic
- Audience problem
- Call to action
- Supporting research
- Distribution plan
- Publication date

### Deliverable

A 30-day content calendar.

### Sources

Kyle Poyar. *How to Build a B2B Content Engine.* Growth Unhinged. 18 September 2024.

https://www.growthunhinged.com/p/how-to-build-a-b2b-content-engine

Jason Lemkin. *10 Things That Always Work in Marketing.* SaaStr. 2024.

https://www.saastr.com/10-things-that-always-work-in-marketing-with-saastr-founder-and-ceo-jason-lemkin-part-1-pod-652-video/

---

## Step 6: Research Before Writing

### Objective

Support important recommendations with evidence.

### Actions

For each recommendation, ask:

- Where did this claim come from?
- What evidence supports it?
- Is there an opposing point of view?
- What are the limitations of the evidence?

Use:

- Customer interviews
- Expert opinions
- Case studies
- Internal experiments
- Industry reports

### Deliverable

A source-backed research brief.

### Sources

Mario Gabriele. *No Rivals: The Prophet — Founders Fund, Part I.* The Generalist. 12 June 2025.

https://www.generalist.com/p/founders-fund-1

First Round Review. *The Ultimate Guide to Writing Great Case Studies.* 10 March 2016.

https://review.firstround.com/the-ultimate-guide-to-writing-great-case-studies/

---

## Step 7: Use a Repeatable Newsletter Framework

### Objective

Make each edition clear, useful, and actionable.

### Recommended Structure

1. Introduce the reader's problem with a strong opening.
2. Explain why the problem matters.
3. Support the argument with evidence or examples.
4. Present a framework or recommended solution.
5. Give the reader clear next steps.
6. End with a relevant call to action.

### Deliverable

A completed newsletter draft.

### Note

This structure is my synthesis based on recurring patterns in the reviewed content. The source below supports using an intentional and repeatable content system but does not prescribe this exact sequence.

### Source

Emily Kramer. *A Behind the Scenes Look at My Content Strategy — Part 1.* MKT1 Newsletter. 6 May 2025.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/mkt1-content-strategy-part-1

---

## Step 8: Publish Consistently

### Objective

Build audience expectations and long-term trust.

### Recommendation

Begin with a weekly or fortnightly schedule. Test whether the cadence can be sustained without reducing quality.

### Deliverable

A documented publishing schedule.

### Source

Jason Lemkin. *Scaling from $1M to $10M: An AMA.* SaaStr. 2023.

https://www.saastr.com/scaling-from-1-to-10m-an-ama-with-saastr-ceo-and-founder-jason-lemkin-pod-573/

---

## Step 9: Repurpose Each Newsletter

### Objective

Extend the value of each edition across multiple channels.

### Actions

Adapt each newsletter into:

- LinkedIn posts
- X threads
- Carousels
- Blog articles
- Short-form videos
- Webinars
- Sales-enablement material

### Deliverable

A repurposing and distribution checklist.

### Note

The specific formats above are my operational recommendation. The source supports building a systematic content operation rather than creating isolated pieces.

### Source

Emily Kramer. *A Behind the Scenes Look at My Content Strategy — Part 1.* MKT1 Newsletter. 6 May 2025.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/mkt1-content-strategy-part-1

---

## Step 10: Measure and Improve

### Objective

Evaluate newsletter health and business impact.

### Newsletter Metrics

- Subscriber growth
- Open rate
- Click-through rate
- Replies
- Referrals

### Business Metrics

- Qualified leads
- Pipeline influenced
- Revenue influenced

### Actions

Review performance monthly and identify:

- Topics to continue
- Formats to improve
- Experiments to run
- Activities to stop

### Deliverable

A monthly newsletter performance report.

### Sources

Kyle Poyar. *50,000 🎉 — How I Grew This Newsletter Over the Past Three Years.* Growth Unhinged. 10 July 2024.

https://www.growthunhinged.com/p/50000

Emily Kramer. *MKT1 Guide to Annual Marketing Planning.* MKT1 Newsletter. 23 September 2024.

https://newsletter.mkt1.co/p/annual-marketing-planning

